  <s:String x:Key="Tip.RecipeRow">Solution "{0}" ({1}), {2} changes. Click for its values in the recipes panel</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.RemoveRoot">Remove the selected folder from the list (files are not touched)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.Rename">Emitter name: Latin letters, digits, “_”. Enter accepts, Esc cancels</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.ResetLayout">Put the panels back where they are by default</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.Restart">Start the effect again from time zero</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.Rnd">Spread: the game takes a value from the base to base + spread (measured in P3)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.Roots">Folders that material and texture paths start from (the work drive, a mod folder). When a path is not found, the folder is looked for from the effect's location</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.Ruler">Time ruler in seconds: click or drag to go there, with Shift to set the work area</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.ScriptRun">{0} "{1}": from {2} to {3} s</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.Search">Find a property by its plain name, game key or description (Ctrl+F); the properties panel keeps the matches</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.Section">Collapse or expand; a collapsed section shows the values from the file</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.Seed">Random seed: the same seed and step give the same particles</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.Shell.hit">The hit shell: damage is dealt inside it</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.Shell.pull">The pull shell: inside it everything is drawn to the centre</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.Shell.sense">The "notices" shell: how near a player or a thrown item makes the anomaly react</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.Sky">Scene light. Noon is taken from the game (R0 capture); dusk and night are approximate and not measured in the game</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.SlicerByAnim">A particle lives frames / fps seconds, LifeTime is ignored (LifetimeByAnim; needs fps above 0)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.SlicerCenterX">Sprite shift across, in half sizes, −1…1 (CenterX): 1 puts the particle at the picture's left edge</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.SlicerCenterY">Sprite shift up and down, in half sizes, −1…1 (CenterY): 1 puts the particle at the picture's top edge, the sprite below it</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.SlicerCentre">The sprite's shift from the particle: X and Y in half sizes, −1…1 (CenterX, CenterY)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.SlicerDefault">The game's values: centre 0 0, scale 1 1</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.SlicerFps">Frames per second (the emitter's AnimFPS, fps). The game plays 0 as 1 frame per second (checked in game). Expressions work: 24, *2, +=4</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.SlicerFramePx">One frame's size in pixels of the top mip</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.SlicerFramePxFraction">The grid does not divide the picture evenly: frames take fractional pixels and their edges fall between pixels</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.SlicerGrid">The material's frame grid: columns × rows (TileU × TileV in the .emat). Editing writes the material</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.SlicerMetres">The sprite in metres: SizeMultiplier × ScaleX and × ScaleY, before the Size curve and SizeRND</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.SlicerMip">Which detail level to show: 0 is full size, each next one is half as big (how the texture looks from afar)</s:String>
