  <s:String x:Key="Tip.SlicerNumbers">Show frame numbers in the game's order</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.SlicerOnce">Not in a loop: a particle that reaches the last frame keeps it until it dies (AnimOnce)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.SlicerOrder">Checked in game (P0, P2): every frame in turn, AnimOnce keeps the last, LifetimeByAnim = frames / fps. The viewport and the slicer pick the frame with the same function</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.SlicerPlay">Play or stop the slicer's sample particles (the viewport plays on its own)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.SlicerRandom">Each particle starts at a random frame (RandomFrame). Without it all start at frame 0: the game has no "start frame" key</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.SlicerSample">A sample particle: shows once the texture is read</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.SlicerSampleAt">Sample {0}: age {1} s, frame {2} (started at {3})</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.SlicerSampleHeld">Sample {0}: age {1} s, frame {2} — the last one, kept until death (started at {3})</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.SlicerScale">Sprite width and height as shares of its size, 0.1…1 (ScaleX, ScaleY)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.SlicerScaleX">Sprite width as a share of its size, 0.1…1 (ScaleX)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.SlicerScaleY">Sprite height as a share of its size, 0.1…1 (ScaleY)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.SlicerSheet">Frames in the game's order: row by row, left to right from the top-left. Cyan frame: the one the first sample particle shows now; violet: the picked frame (shown on the right); yellow count: live viewport particles on that frame now. Click to pick a frame</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.SlicerSpeed">How much slower to play the samples to look at the frames. Does not change the file</s:String>
