  <s:String x:Key="Tip.FirstFrame">Length of the frame right after the effect appears, in seconds (0 = a normal step). The first time a player's game shows an effect that is not registered in ParticleList it loads it, and that frame is long (measured 0.137 s): short one-shot emitters then lose their particles. Registered particles are loaded when the game starts. At most 0.3 s, like the game</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.Stress">Stress test: copies of the effect in a grid; particle count and frame time in the viewport corner</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.Sub.Accept">Use the proposed file as the substitute</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.Sub.AcceptAll">Write every proposal found into the table</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.Sub.Check">Find missing textures in every effect of the sources, with proposals</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.Sub.Gone">the substitute file is gone: {0}</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.Sub.NoProposal">Pick a file yourself (File…)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.Sub.Pick">Pick the substitute file yourself</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.Sub.Proposal">Accept writes this proposal</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="Tip.Sub.Remove">Remove the substitute from the table</s:String>
